WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:01.840
- For many of us working from home

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:04.310
has become a reality over the last months.

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:07.610
But clearly home office is not
without its own challenges.

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:10.080
Direct interaction with
your colleagues and clients

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.080
is now much harder than before.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:14.420
Also you need to motivate yourself

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:15.930
and find your new rhythm

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:18.170
while working at home the whole day.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:20.580
On top of that, I recently
conducted a survey

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:22.150
on my LinkedIn page,

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:25.770
asking you whether working
from home has improved

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:29.580
or not improved your
subjective work-life balance.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.480
And here I must say, it
was quite interesting

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:33.830
for me to see that almost half of you

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:37.020
said that working from
home actually worsened

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:39.480
your subjective work-life balance.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.300
So welcome to another Coffee Break

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.410
here on my channel, Firm Learning.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.230
My name is Heinrich, and on my channel

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:47.630
I want to help you to become successful

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:49.880
in the first years of your career.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:51.000
And in today's video,

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.570
we are indeed going talk
about working from home,

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:57.070
about home office, and I want
to share with you three tips.

00:00:57.070 --> 00:01:00.470
What you can do to improve
your working from home,

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.210
home office experience.

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:03.470
But before we jump into it,

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:06.410
let me introduce you to the
sponsor of this week's video,

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:07.510
Vidyard.

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:09.490
Vidyard is a free to use online tool,

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:11.510
which is designed for young professionals,

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:14.970
among others to review goals
and align projects with their

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:17.720
colleagues and just
making working from home

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:18.670
easier for them.

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:20.760
But now let's start with the three tips

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:22.110
and let's get into it.

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:24.380
The first tip is on how you communicate

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:25.720
while working from home.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:28.330
And let me start by
reflecting on the differences,

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:31.090
from being co-located in an office

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:32.961
with your colleagues or clients,

00:01:32.961 --> 00:01:35.020
or there's working from
home and not having

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:37.600
this direct interaction with
your clients or colleagues.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:39.700
Because indeed what you
can do if you're on a call

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:43.150
located in one office,
is just walk by the desk

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:46.350
of one of your colleagues,
have an informal conversation,

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:49.240
invite them to a coffee
and just talk to them.

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:51.710
And any of those members of
the Firm Learning community

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:54.140
who have watched this channel
since the very beginning

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:56.280
might have also seen this video on the

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:01.060
golden consulting rule,
which is walk, talk, write.

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:03.750
So in the old times you
were told that usually

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:06.410
you should always try to walk by a client,

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:08.270
to directly talk to the person.

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:11.130
If that's not possible,
you try to talk to them

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.700
on the phone, for instance,
just calling them.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.160
And only if this is not possible this way,

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.860
only then you write to them.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:19.850
And I hope the reasons are quite obvious.

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:21.360
If you want to refresh on that,

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.980
I will link this video
somewhere above here for you

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:24.820
to check it out.

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:27.380
But clearly now in the
times of working from home,

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:30.150
the walk option is now
not possible anymore.

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:33.610
And also talking is more
difficult because you cannot have

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:35.870
these more informal conversations.

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:38.490
You will need to always
schedule a meeting,

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:41.920
book an appointment, to
then jump on a video chat

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:44.350
with one of these people, if
this is what you want to do.

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:47.040
So to overcome this, at
least to some extent,

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:49.760
one thing that really made
a difference in the company

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:52.510
where I currently work for
as chief revenue officer,

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:55.480
are tricks that help you to in a quick

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:57.670
and very straightforward way,

00:02:57.670 --> 00:03:01.050
create videos about you
talking, create videos

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:04.170
where you can show certain
things, how you do things,

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:05.600
add explanations,

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:08.110
and then share these videos
with your colleagues.

00:03:08.110 --> 00:03:09.858
But now think about that,

00:03:09.858 --> 00:03:12.210
like typically the hurdles
to do this are quite big.

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:14.030
While your laptop might have a webcam,

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:17.400
you will usually need
specialized recording software

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:18.560
to create videos.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:22.000
Then you will need editing
software to combine the videos

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:25.320
with maybe some other picture
feeds or screen recording

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:28.250
feeds for which you might need
additional software as well,

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:29.830
just to then create the video.

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:31.670
And then you will
usually need some type of

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:34.050
hosting solution where
then you can distribute

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:36.370
the video too, and then
share it from there.

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:39.400
This of course makes it
quite complicated and really

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:42.680
increases the hurdles of
creating videos for you to really

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:45.900
share with your team and
just simplify communication.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:48.770
Therefore, I'm very happy
that the creators of Vidyard

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:51.630
decided to sponsor this
video on this topic,

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:54.840
and they have also contributed
to this channel because they

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:58.180
created a tool that helps
you to do exactly that.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:01.500
They have a Chrome extension,
which is free to use,

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:05.050
which you can use to very
easily create videos of yours,

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:07.740
potentially also picture-in-picture videos

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:11.190
where both your screen and
your picture feed is recorded,

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:13.681
where you can then really
show certain things.

00:04:13.681 --> 00:04:16.040
Let's imagine you have a big XM model

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:18.660
where you want to point
out a very specific problem

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:19.590
you are facing.

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:21.390
What I also very much laugh about this

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:23.770
is that this way of
working often helps you

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:25.618
to avoid unnecessary meetings

00:04:25.618 --> 00:04:28.830
because now instead of you
just scheduling a meeting

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:32.320
and then blocking this time
in both or all the calendars

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:34.680
that are involved, now you
can just create a video

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:37.480
and then everybody can
watch it at their own

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:39.770
schedule, whenever they
have the time to do so.

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:41.710
But now, instead of me talking about it,

