00:07:38.260 --> 00:07:40.270
Tip number two that I would
like to share with you

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:43.005
is learning from meeting cadences

00:07:43.005 --> 00:07:44.350
that were frequently used in consulting

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:46.930
and how these could apply
to you, to your team,

00:07:46.930 --> 00:07:49.860
to really help you to
work together more closely

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:51.770
with your team in the
times of home office,

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:55.250
where you cannot just walk
by your team's office,

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:57.090
just talking to your colleagues

00:07:57.090 --> 00:07:58.380
if you have a simple question.

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:00.810
And specifically the format
that I'm talking about is

00:08:00.810 --> 00:08:03.960
daily team check-ins and
daily team check-outs.

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:06.690
So this is a format that was
very frequently applied in

00:08:06.690 --> 00:08:08.900
consulting, so as the project lead,

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:11.170
you would set up every single morning,

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:13.907
usually around 8:30 am
or something like that.

00:08:13.907 --> 00:08:16.900
The team check-in where
everyone from your project team

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:20.790
comes together, shares his or
her priorities for the day,

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:22.860
discusses what all the
individual consultants

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:25.220
are working on and
potentially also get input

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:27.900
from other teammates
that might be relevant

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:30.280
to the tasks of other
colleagues in the team.

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:32.750
From my experience, this
proved highly effective

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:35.680
to align everyone on the
mission and make sure

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:37.750
that all the important
tasks are worked on.

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:41.010
And in a similar way, the daily
check-outs are being used.

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:43.400
Rather usually around 5 or 6:00 pm,

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:45.310
you would come together with your team,

00:08:45.310 --> 00:08:47.650
everybody would give an
update what they have been

00:08:47.650 --> 00:08:50.360
working on, and potentially
also what they intend

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:53.010
to still work on later in the evening.

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:55.480
And of course, then this
also as a project lead

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:58.170
might be used as an opportunity
for you to potentially

00:08:58.170 --> 00:09:01.890
help some of your teammates
to reprioritize their tasks,

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:04.340
if you feel like a person
would have still lots of work

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:06.750
to do that evening,
maybe you can just talk

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:08.770
and understand what the
things are that really

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:12.370
need to be done this evening,
what maybe the things are

00:09:12.370 --> 00:09:16.050
that also have time to be
completed tomorrow or the next day

00:09:16.050 --> 00:09:18.270
or later that week to
make sure that everybody's

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:20.750
not having too much of a
hard time during the day.

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:23.849
And especially in my last
role after consulting,

00:09:23.849 --> 00:09:26.860
where I worked as a CTO
in a SME German retailer,

00:09:26.860 --> 00:09:29.300
once we were hurt by
the new health situation

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:31.040
that started last year,

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:34.620
this is really what we
started to do every single day

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:36.090
in the leadership team,

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:39.550
this daily check-in, just
to get us all updated.

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:41.950
This really worked very, very well for us.

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:43.830
And I would just encourage
you to check this out,

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:45.510
try this out for your team as well,

00:09:45.510 --> 00:09:47.990
if this is not yet something
that you already do.

00:09:47.990 --> 00:09:51.440
The third tip that I have for
you is to reflect on your team

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:53.360
norms and team values

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:56.390
while now moving into this
new direction of home office

00:09:56.390 --> 00:09:57.640
and working from home.

00:09:57.640 --> 00:10:00.000
It seems to be very
obvious, at least to me,

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.530
that if you want to be
successful as a team

00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:04.100
in this new environment,

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:07.590
you cannot just continue with
the team norms and team values

00:10:07.590 --> 00:10:10.230
that you had, and that
maybe also worked very well

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:12.640
for you prior to this new situation.

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:15.270
What worked quite well for me
in the past is to get together

00:10:15.270 --> 00:10:18.660
with your team and do a session
where you all reflect on

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:21.720
what the new norms, what the new rules are

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:24.250
that you will need as a team to succeed.

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:27.300
Let me share one very
specific example from my prior

00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:32.300
conversations, and this was the
value of over-communication.

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:33.760
So in my last role,

00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:37.330
we came together and came to
the conclusion that a crucial

00:10:37.330 --> 00:10:41.800
new norm that we wanted to
establish was over-communication.

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:43.840
And this was created out
of the observation that

00:10:43.840 --> 00:10:45.913
after a couple of months,

00:10:45.913 --> 00:10:48.520
we realized that the number
of misunderstandings,

00:10:48.520 --> 00:10:52.220
the number of miscommunications
seemed to have increased

00:10:52.220 --> 00:10:53.740
due to the new situation.

00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:56.210
Clearly, if you struggle
to really talk to people

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:58.870
face-to-face, it might
be more difficult to you

00:10:58.870 --> 00:11:00.870
to also reach out, look for these more

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:03.700
informal communications,
maybe just check-ins

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:05.780
at the coffee bar, but you can just have

00:11:05.780 --> 00:11:08.620
a brief conversation with
your colleague asking

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:10.930
if all the things you
discussed in the last meeting

00:11:10.930 --> 00:11:12.050
were well understood.

00:11:12.050 --> 00:11:14.650
These things are of course, missing now.

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:16.840
And it is even more important therefore,

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:20.360
to compensate this and
to communicate even more

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:23.730
namely to over-communicate
as we have then called it.

00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:26.640
And specifically what this
meant is that the responsibility

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:30.290
on a task being understood,
on an important point being

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:32.900
shared and reflected
by everyone on the team

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:36.225
is now even more on the
sender, on the communicator

00:11:36.225 --> 00:11:37.470
than before.

00:11:37.470 --> 00:11:40.490
And here I also made the
experience that a tool like Vidyard

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:42.630
can really be tremendously helpful

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:45.720
to avoid miscommunication,
because instead of just writing

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:47.980
a message or maybe saying
something in a meeting,

00:11:47.980 --> 00:11:50.670
you can share your thoughts in a video,

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:54.480
actually sharing what you
mean and showing what you mean

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:56.280
with very little effort.

00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:58.300
So for instance, one
thing that you could do is

00:11:58.300 --> 00:12:02.480
after a meeting, you can record
your main points in a video,

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:05.270
potentially also show exactly
the things that you mean,

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:06.730
maybe in a document,

00:12:06.730 --> 00:12:09.420
in a file on some webpage on the internet,

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:12.320
and then share this
video with the teammates

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:14.310
that you're working on, just to make sure

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:17.200
that you are over-communicating indeed

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:20.190
and avoid any
misunderstandings on the team.

00:12:20.190 --> 00:12:23.740
I trust that this can go a
very long way and really bring

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:27.760
you together and making sure
that you can work also remotely

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:29.340
in a highly effective way.

